{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788264860,"nonce":"KbbIJMA8hTOErTyUDdqccrfX7sU=","message":"RULING: **this issue does NOT close.** Session 13, orchestrator.\n\nThe Acceptance section is the definition of done, and its first bullet reads:\n\n\u003e ≥2 of 3 colonists alive at day 10 without post-staging dev intervention.\n\n**2 of 3 were dead on day 4.** The run stopped on day 6 of 10. No amount of platform success changes that line, and the third bullet — Dorian signs off after reviewing the run — is a gate on a passing run, not a mechanism for passing a failed one. A spec is a contract; this one failed its own hard criterion, so it stays open and M1 re-runs.\n\nWhat the run DID prove is real and is not lost by staying open: 0 red errors across 175 journal events, a clean no-dev-verbs proof (last `dev` row at tick 723, all 50 dev rows there), the clothes check firing and journalled, and the first time in this project's history that the 4.2 auditor ran against a real run. `RUNS/m1-20260831/` is the evidence and stands as the record. The platform passed. The colony failed. Those are separate verdicts and only the second one is this issue's acceptance.\n\n## The re-run is GATED, not merely pending\n\nRe-running now would reproduce the same deaths, because every cause is still live. The four fixes the run itself produced are filed, and each is a dependency of the re-run:\n\n- `40ed42f` — **doctor coverage**, `work_coverage` in the digest with Doctor's floor at 2, plus the roster-change repair. The only pawn with Doctor enabled was the first casualty. Extended by post-mortem OUT-3 with the casualty-triage procedure and forced `rescue`.\n- `722c951` — **`advance` refuses on an unread journal**, extended by OUT-1 to also halt on an own-faction downing or death. The run made 27 advances and ZERO `journal` calls; Table's downing was announced inside an advance result and the run advanced again.\n- `b1b3060` — **the posture verb.** Allowed area, seek ON, `hostility:\"Attack\"` as one act instead of three things to remember in the right order. Turning seek off silently put three unarmed pawns back on the flee branch, and Captain fled 150 cells into unexplored ground and died there.\n- `61794cd` — **the bleed-out clock, and the hediff cap that hid it.** `BloodLoss` was cut from all four of Captain's health reads by the 20-row cap. The surface truncated away the thing that was killing him.\n\nThose four are the same four the run's own fix list named, now specified rather than remembered. Add `1adc737` (build verbs) to the list of things to settle first — see the separate comment there; the no-build-verb finding made the whole work surface shallow and made a single silent staging refusal permanent.\n\n## What changed on THIS issue's acceptance\n\nBullet 3's `final-undrafted` criterion is amended per Evan's ruling of 2026-09-01 — see the escalation comment above. It now reads **0 drafted, 0 hostiles that have not been pardoned**, where a pardon is a journalled act with a required reason. `threat-pardon` and the `hostiles_pardoned` / `hostiles_unpardoned` digest fields shipped this session.\n\nBullet 2 — \"the deliverables above committed; spec-gap comments filed\" — is now DONE, and was not before: run report, the post-mortem in full (`RUNS/m1-20260831/postmortem.md`), four playbook lessons all now cited by a checklist, and the spec-gap list filed as comments on the issues it belongs to.\n\n## Labelling\n\nMoving to `state:blocked` rather than `state:next`. It is not waiting on someone to pick it up; it is waiting on four specs, and starting it before they land would spend a ten-day run reproducing a known result.","files":null}]}